  "method": [
    "Unchanged frozen guest kernel and applications. Two default runs, two runs with only capstone_vm.node_initial_pages=36, and one negative detector run. All exact GCC outputs match.",
    "Single-vCPU plugin counts every guest instruction attempt and brackets ensure_nodes and node_add_page at entry/return. This includes their callees and any intervening interrupt work. Both symbols and return instructions are resolved from the exact Image/System.map.",
    "Existing independent phase plugin agrees on all function-entry counts and its phase totals sum to profrun total. Growth sequences and inclusive counts agree across repeats.",
    "A separate GDB register/memory trace confirms table capacities, requested headroom and successful returns for both growths; breakpoint-run timing is not used.",
    "Negative control disables the ensure_nodes entry marker: the detector reports 381 orphan returns and is rejected, while GCC output still matches."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Inclusive handler counts exclude the triggering task transition/retry outside ensure_nodes; whole-run preallocation control includes these effects but also moves allocation work to startup.",
    "The approximately 0.006 percent whole-run reduction is tiny and sensitive to short-run kernel variation; it is not an established elapsed-time speedup.",
    "Initial node_add_page counts exclude allocating the root page and other task/context setup. Final table footprint adds the root separately.",
    "Allocation and growth are not lifetime-table lookup, per-access validation, cache behavior, or a flat-versus-paged comparison.",
    "Sites and context+32 table-pointer layout are tied to the recorded kernel. The diagnostic addresses must be regenerated/audited for another kernel.",
    "No collection call occurred in these GCC runs; this result does not measure namespace-recycling cost."
  ],
